1064:- Requirements (revision 18, D153): R4, R42 and R43 say what D149 and D153 decided and 9042fb4 and 7c8fba2 build, so no log format, stored data, table or committed figure changes. The frozen check moves no shipped verdict: v1 loads as before, by its pinned hash, and v2 passes every check. A save the file system fails stores nothing new; under the revision 18 default T12 maps the error at four more call sites, which changes only what the caller is told.
1065:- Requirements (revision 19, D158): R4, R42, R54 and P15 say what D154 and D158 decided and 9c265a3, 51c8b68 and 7cb2e71 build, so no log format, stored data, table or committed figure changes. The shipped v1 matches its pin, so comparing its bytes first changes nothing for it, and v2 holds no malformed value. A save refused partway through its line leaves what a crash leaves, which the existing repair drops; under the revision 19 default T12 carries the error out of six reads, which changes only what the caller is told.
1116:- **The signal for the case log (revisions 5 to 21):** `cma case check` per case gives one of three outcomes. Intact: exit 0, only from a reader that found the case free. Being saved or not checked: exit 4, with the recorded entries that check out, nothing checked yet, or the lock error named. A bad entry: exit 3, with the first bad or incomplete entry by number, a recorded entry cut short, a lost head record or a log that two saves told recorded at one position left included. A writer refused because another holds the case says so ('another window or command is writing to this case') and writes nothing. A writer refused because a lock file, the gate or the case lock, was removed or replaced says so: 'a case lock file was removed or replaced while this window held the case', followed by 'nothing was written' and that the save was not recorded or, once any part of the line is written, 'part of its entry was written and the save was not recorded' (revision 19), or, refused at the head rename, 'its entry was written and the save was not recorded' (revision 20). No message about a save whose line is in the log says nothing was written. A save refused because another save is under way in the same window, or because the log changed since its check or while it was being recorded, says so and asks to reload. A save whose head record was not taken back after a failed read-back says that whether the save is in the log is not confirmed, names what stopped the take-back in its own words, and asks for the case log to be checked before anything else is saved (R42 since revision 17, D143; one answer since revision 21, D168). A save the file system failed names the error and says the save was not recorded or, when its head record was published and not taken back, that whether it is in the log is not confirmed (R42 since revision 18; one rule since revision 19). No message, and no error it carries, gives a second answer (revision 21). So does a save whose own check could not read the log, the head record or a lock file, and it never says the case changed or a lock file was removed or replaced (revision 20). If the friend sees the first with only one window open, or the second at all, something outside the tool is touching the case folder (a share, a forked process, a stuck command, a sync or backup client, a cleanup script), and the trial sheet says to move the case to a plain local folder.
1118:- **Log lines:** one structured line per event in the case log, with the event, case id, snapshot and counts, and no names or descriptions. For example: event=pack_written traced=100 reconciled=true unexplained_pct=12.4 ambiguous=4 cash_flagged=3 policy_check=shown.
